# End of every session, update four files

Do this before ending a session in which anything was committed. Do not wait to be asked.

Each file answers a different question, so write to that question rather than repeating the same
summary four times.

1. **`SESSION.md`** — *what changed and why?* Add a new dated entry at the top. Cover what changed
   and *why*, the resulting state, and what is still open. Write it for someone who was not present.
   Carry forward any open item that is still open; delete ones that were resolved.
2. **`ROLLBACK.md`** — *what do I go back to?* Add every new commit to the `dev` or production table
   with its short SHA, date and summary. Update the "Current state" table. If a commit is a sensible
   rollback target or a known-bad point, note it under "Known-good checkpoints".
3. **`confluence.md`** — *how does it behave now?* Only where behaviour actually changed. Update the
   affected section, plus the env var table, cache-key table, or data-source table if those moved.
   It is a maintenance reference, not a changelog: describe how the system works now, not what
   changed.
4. **`README.md`** — *what is this and how do I work on it?* The entry point for someone new to the
   repository. Update it only when the tech stack, external connectivity, setup steps, repository
   layout or development workflow actually changed — or when a new trap is worth warning people
   about in "Maintenance notes". Most sessions will not touch it, and that is correct; it is
   orientation, not a changelog. Keep detail in `confluence.md` and link to it rather than
   duplicating, so the two cannot drift.

Verify SHAs with `git log --format='%h|%ci|%s'` rather than writing them from memory.

# Branch discipline

- Production is `main`, deployed automatically on push, and is in active use.
- Development happens on `dev`, which deploys as an isolated Vercel preview.
- Never push feature work directly to `main`. Ship with `git checkout main && git merge dev`.
- Do not commit unrelated files. This repo usually carries uncommitted churn in
  `data/*.sqlite*`, `scripts/import_aom_to_sqlite.py`, `data/README-aom-import.md` and `.DS_Store` —
  leave it alone.
- Four files carry CRLF line endings (`lib/map-stress-utils.ts`, `app/actions/cre-deterioration.ts`,
  `app/actions/export-market-analytics-report.ts`, `lib/noncurrent-debug.ts`). Editing them with a
  script in text mode rewrites every line and buries the real change. Check `git show --stat` before
  pushing.

# Environment detection

Never use `process.env.NODE_ENV` to detect production. Vercel sets it to `"production"` on preview
builds too, so a dev deployment is indistinguishable from the live tool. Use `lib/environment.ts`:

```ts
import { isProductionDeployment, assertSafeToMutateProductionData } from "@/lib/environment"
```

Call `assertSafeToMutateProductionData("...")` before any irreversible write, and map the thrown
`ProductionDataWriteError` to a 403. See `docs/DEV_ENVIRONMENT.md`.
